## Lore

Project Achilles looked at rodents for their hardiness and staying power rather
than their bite, and one line blended human, rat and capybara, the largest
rodent alive and a strong swimmer native to South America. The result was a
tough, amphibious mutant that turned out to be a powerful psychic as well.

Its gifts let it breathe water and shrug off harsh conditions, but the rarest of
them touch dimensional energy itself: sending messages and jumping along ley
lines, bending time, loosing a stunning wave of psychic force, and at high
levels crossing between worlds. Many capybaras leave Achilles for years to
wander the Megaverse, and groups of them can close Rifts or call up ley line
storms.

Seeing what others cannot gives the race a mystical bent. Capybaras tend to be
unhurried philosophers, full of patient sayings, and their reputation for
wisdom and moderation puts many of them in the Animal House. Those who serve in
the army often double as medics, especially if they have healing powers.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'mutant-capybara');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'mutant-capybara';

